---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="License | Data Science Judgment Lab">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open Source</p>
      <h1>Free to inspect, adapt, and teach from.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Data Science Judgment Lab is an open-source educational project. The
        code is reusable under MIT, and the case materials are available for
        noncommercial educational use with attribution.
      </p>

      <h2>Split License</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Project Part</th>
            <th>License</th>
            <th>What That Means</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Site code, styles, scripts, scoring logic, and components</td>
            <td>MIT</td>
            <td>May be reused, modified, forked, and redistributed with the license notice.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Cases, evidence packets, replays, instructor notes, and written curriculum</td>
            <td>CC BY-NC 4.0</td>
            <td>May be reused and adapted for noncommercial purposes with attribution.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Why This Structure</h2>
      <p>
        The lab is built around transparent pedagogy: learners and instructors
        should be able to inspect how the cases, scoring, and calibration record
        work. At the same time, the case library represents substantial
        curriculum design work, so commercial reuse of the case content requires
        separate permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Source</h2>
      <p>
        The source repository is available on GitHub:
        <a href="https://github.com/stuartjonesstats/data-science-judgment-lab">Data Science Judgment Lab</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For full legal terms, see the repository license files:
        <a href="https://github.com/stuartjonesstats/data-science-judgment-lab/blob/main/LICENSE.md">license summary</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/stuartjonesstats/data-science-judgment-lab/blob/main/LICENSE-CODE">MIT code license</a>,
        and
        <a href="https://github.com/stuartjonesstats/data-science-judgment-lab/blob/main/LICENSE-CONTENT.md">content license notice</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
